[2026-01-30T13:05:50.470Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RsAdo4VQGgwVR9yNCxbXFb","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n     2→\n     3→## REQUIREMENT\n     4→\n     5→# Virtualize FindingsTab list for large datasets\n     6→\n     7→## Metadata\n     8→- **Category**: performance\n     9→- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n    10→- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n    11→- **Scan Type**: perf_optimizer\n    12→- **Generated**: 1/30/2026, 1:35:36 AM\n    13→\n    14→## Description\n    15→FindingsTab renders all findings with expandable FindingCard components. For reports with 100+ findings, this creates significant DOM bloat. Implement react-window virtualization to only render visible findings, keeping DOM light and scrolling smooth.\n    16→\n    17→## Reasoning\n    18→Research sessions can accumulate hundreds of findings. Rendering all of them degrades scroll performance and increases memory usage. Virtualization reduces DOM nodes from O(n) to O(viewport), making large reports feel as fast as small ones.\n    19→\n    20→## Context\n    21→\n    22→**Note**: This section provides supporting architectural documentation and is NOT a hard requirement. Use it as guidance to understand existing code structure and maintain consistency.\n    23→\n    24→### Context: Report Tabs\n    25→\n    26→**Description**: Tab-based navigation components for quick-access report sections. Provides compact, scannable summaries for overview, findings, sources, entities, analysis, and perspectives.\n    27→**Related Files**:\n    28→- `src/components/report/tabs/OverviewTab.tsx`\n    29→- `src/components/report/tabs/FindingsTab.tsx`\n    30→- `src/components/report/tabs/SourcesTab.tsx`\n    31→- `src/components/report/tabs/EntitiesTab.tsx`\n    32→- `src/components/report/tabs/AnalysisTab.tsx`\n    33→- `src/components/report/tabs/PerspectivesTab.tsx`\n    34→- `src/components/report/tabs/index.tsx`\n    35→\n    36→**Post-Implementation**: After completing this requirement, evaluate if the context description or file paths need updates. Use the appropriate API/DB query to update the context if architectural changes were made.\n    37→\n    38→## Recommended Skills\n    39→\n    40→- **compact-ui-design**: Use `.claude/skills/compact-ui-design.md` for high-quality UI design references and patterns\n    41→\n    42→## Notes\n    43→\n    44→This requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n    45→\n    46→## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n    47→\n    48→1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n    49→   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n    50→   - title: 2-6 word summary\n    51→   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n    52→\n    53→2. Check for test scenario using `check_test_scenario` MCP tool\n    54→   - If hasScenario is true, call `capture_screenshot` tool\n    55→   - If hasScenario is false, skip screenshot\n    56→\n    57→3. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n    58→\n    59→Begin implementation now.\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9cec20cb-b613-4ab4-b437-0d4075a2df3d","uuid":"97e3fae8-64df-4a98-84d0-87945b339803","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\.claude\\commands\\idea-c7487854-virtualize-findingstab-list-fo.md","content":"Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n\n## REQUIREMENT\n\n# Virtualize FindingsTab list for large datasets\n\n## Metadata\n- **Category**: performance\n- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Scan Type**: perf_optimizer\n- **Generated**: 1/30/2026, 1:35:36 AM\n\n## Description\nFindingsTab renders all findings with expandable FindingCard components. For reports with 100+ findings, this creates significant DOM bloat. Implement react-window virtualization to only render visible findings, keeping DOM light and scrolling smooth.\n\n## Reasoning\nResearch sessions can accumulate hundreds of findings. Rendering all of them degrades scroll performance and increases memory usage. Virtualization reduces DOM nodes from O(n) to O(viewport), making large reports feel as fast as small ones.\n\n## Context\n\n**Note**: This section provides supporting architectural documentation and is NOT a hard requirement. Use it as guidance to understand existing code structure and maintain consistency.\n\n### Context: Report Tabs\n\n**Description**: Tab-based navigation components for quick-access report sections. Provides compact, scannable summaries for overview, findings, sources, entities, analysis, and perspectives.\n**Related Files**:\n- `src/components/report/tabs/OverviewTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/FindingsTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/SourcesTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/EntitiesTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/AnalysisTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/PerspectivesTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/index.tsx`\n\n**Post-Implementation**: After completing this requirement, evaluate if the context description or file paths need updates. Use the appropriate API/DB query to update the context if architectural changes were made.\n\n## Recommended Skills\n\n- **compact-ui-design**: Use `.claude/skills/compact-ui-design.md` for high-quality UI design references and patterns\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n\n## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n\n1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n   - title: 2-6 word summary\n   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n\n2. Check for test scenario using `check_test_scenario` MCP tool\n   - If hasScenario is true, call `capture_screenshot` tool\n   - If hasScenario is false, skip screenshot\n\n3. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n\nBegin implementation now.","numLines":59,"startLine":1,"totalLines":59}}}
